                {"question": "Why is using Cells(Rows.Count, 1).End(xlUp).Row to find the last row better than hardcoding a row number like 100?", "options": ["It is not actually better, hardcoding is always preferred", "It dynamically finds the true last row of data, so the macro works correctly regardless of how many rows exist", "Hardcoded numbers run faster in all cases", "This formula only works for exactly 100 rows"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Dynamic last-row detection makes a macro robust to changing dataset sizes rather than breaking or under/over-processing rows."},
