                {"question": "What does pressing F8 in the VBA Editor do?", "options": ["Deletes the current macro", "Runs the macro one line at a time (Step Into), allowing you to watch behavior as it executes", "Immediately runs the entire macro with no pausing", "Opens a new blank module"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "F8 executes VBA code one statement at a time, letting you observe exactly where unexpected behavior occurs."},
